END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Power of the Pen: Handwriting Analysis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T140000
UID:6a85e6a160ccaf01c01f64e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come prepared to laugh and learn during Elaine's "Power of the
  Pen" while you discover how to communicate even more effectively with fam
 ily and friends through knowing what the strokes of handwriting mean.  Ev
 eryone will learn about their strengths as reflected in the 'paper mirror'
  of their handwriting.  Elaine will be e-mailing Handwriting Profiles to 
 the Participants who fill out the Handwriting Form!
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e6a160ccaf01c01f64e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moving Stories: Arts-based movement class for older adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T113000
UID:6a26cef0f56bd86e00b548a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Tiger princess dance projects\n\, a non-profit contemporary da
 nce company\, brings you a free custom designed arts-based movement class 
 for older adults. Join Artistic Director Yvonne Ng and her team of profess
 ional artists in a fun\, healthy\, and exciting arts program\,\nMoving Sto
 ries\n.\nThese free classes offer an introduction into the enriching world
  of art and creativity through movement and music. These activities have p
 roven to improve circulation\, retain joint mobility\, promote mental stim
 ulation\, improve posture and coordination\, and build strength and balanc
 e.\nNo previous movement experience required.\nSuggested Age: 60 +\nGo at 
 your own pace\, modifications encouraged\nExercises can be modified for se
 ated movement and/or standing
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a26cef0f56bd86e00b548a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Letters to Amelia: Author Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T150000
UID:6a7385b73f18b57d52339ed0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Women's History Month with Toronto-based author and
  letter writer Lindsay Zier-Vogel who discusses\n“Letters to Amelia”\
 n\, her debut novel inspired by her passion for Amelia Earhart\, and the p
 ower of reading and writing letters for both connection and self-discovery
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7385b73f18b57d52339ed0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
