BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Edible History of Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
UID:6a7e344ca821f90037eda982@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto is a global culinary capital\, home to iconic food bra
 nds and restaurants\, from Café Diplomatico to Mr. Christie's Cookies. Bu
 t how did Toronto earn its reputation as a foodie haven? Join culinary his
 torian Dr. Laura Carlson on a mouth-watering journey through Toronto’s f
 ood history. Bring your appetite and your stretchy pants for a virtual tas
 te of past and present Toronto.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e344ca821f90037eda982
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
