DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T170000
UID:6a84859f69166f088b930bba@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you 55+? Do you have a phone\, tablet or computer you don'
 t know how to use or want to learn to use better? Do you enjoy meeting new
  people?\nSeniors E-Connect will help you learn tech topics in a fun group
  setting\, but with the one-on-one help of a teen volunteer under the gui
 dance of library staff. Learn the basics of using computers\, tablets and 
 smartphones and popular websites and software.\nIf you're a teen between t
 he ages of 13-17 and would like to learn more about becoming a Seniors E-C
 onnect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E-Connect Volunteering page\nor cont
 act the branch.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Bagshaw Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84859f69166f088b930bba
