BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Use Cellphone and Apps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T153000
UID:6a88d06260ccaf01c02007ed@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we learn about the basics of using a cell phone. In
  this class we will cover all of the different  parts of a basic smart pho
 ne\, the operating system\, the home page and how to use Wi-Fi and Cellula
 r Data. We will practice skills such as taking a picture\, scanning a QR c
 ode\, and sending a text. No prior expertise in cell phone use is required
  to take this class.\nFor people who are new to cell phones and apps and w
 ant a basic understanding of how to use them. No previous experience is re
 quired. In this course we will look at:\n-What is an app?\n-Differences be
 tween pre-installed\, free\, and paid apps\n-Where to find and download ap
 ps\n-How to delete apps\nResource handout provided.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a88d06260ccaf01c02007ed
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drop-In Tech Help
