BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 2: Do More with your Data
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T153000
UID:6a623e3bc7e02e3d006b221d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCreate 
 and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then sort and filter\nCr
 eate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to
  get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPrerequisites
 : Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard sk
 ills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre on the Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a623e3bc7e02e3d006b221d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d62@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nSeptember 5th –\nPapillon (
 1973)\nSeptember 12th –\nCabaret\nSeptember 19th –\nWhat's Eating Gilb
 ert Grape\nSeptember 26th –\nMoonlight\nDrop in\, no registration is req
 uired.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredi
 ent lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaborat
 ion with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d62
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mimico Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T120000
UID:6a873d93db86e4004d867ef0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our book selection for October is\nTitus Groan\nby Mervyn Peak
 e\, an eccentric and epic novel about the inhabitants of a vast\, isolat
 ed castle ruled by the Groan family. By turns fantastical\, comical\, and 
 dramatic\, Groan and its sequel\, Gormenghast\, is regarded as one of the 
 greatest and most unique achievements in fantasy literature.\nCopies avail
 able at the library.\nThe Gormenghast Trilogy
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a873d93db86e4004d867ef0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
