SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T170000
UID:69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Humbermede Neighbourhood Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T194500
UID:6966a7f9c719ac98c336d067@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Humbermede Neighbourhood Community meeting allows neighbou
 rs to come together and discuss or learn about things happening in the com
 munity. Join the conversation\, connect with your neighbourhood community
  groups (e.g. Engage416 representative)\, accessing free resources and ha
 ve your voice heard regarding your concerns\, be part of the solution.
LOCATION:Woodview Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6966a7f9c719ac98c336d067
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newcomer Settlement Services
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260911T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260911T170000
UID:6a47defbe3c2e3fd937c22d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Friday from 9am - 5 pm.\nVisit 
 our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrosscultural.or
 g.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease bring you
 r immigration documents (PR card) with you
LOCATION:Burrows Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a47defbe3c2e3fd937c22d7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canadian Council of the Blind Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T120000
UID:6a3bfbeec52cdc3600ec8366@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This book club is facilitated by staff in partnership with the
  Canadian Council of the Blind\, Toronto Visionaries Chapter. The book clu
 b is open to those living with vision loss or low vision\, or are deaf-bli
 nd and to their sighted support persons. The book club meets on the third 
 Wednesday of the month. October's book is\nWhat Strange Paradise\nby Omar
  el Akkad.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3bfbeec52cdc3600ec8366
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senior's E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T173000
UID:6a56c066fb418a28009b0354@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have questions about your tablet\, phone\, laptop\, ema
 il or an app?  Need help with eBooks or other online library services? We
  can help!\nJoin us for this intergenerational program that pairs teen vol
 unteers with seniors to answer your tech questions.\nDrop in\, no registra
 tion is required. Participants may be limited to 1/2 hr sessions.\nEvery T
 uesday\, from 4:00-5:30 pm. Please note\, in April\, program will run ever
 y Tuesday.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a56c066fb418a28009b0354
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
