X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Royal Conservatory of Music & Telus Centre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T200000
UID:6a832b259d8416003f69c765@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This beautiful 1880s Toronto Baptist College building\, now th
 e Royal Conservatory of Music\, was sensitively restored in the early 21st
  century. The catalyst was the addition of the innovative Telus Centre for
  Performance and Learning. Through dozens of photographs\, architectural h
 istorian Marta O'Brien will discuss the exteriors and interiors of this wo
 nderful complex dedicated to music education and performance.\nDoors open 
 at 6:30pm\nPresented in collaboration with North Toronto Historical Societ
 y.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a832b259d8416003f69c765
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:La Scopa: Learn and Play a Traditional Italian Card Game
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T150000
UID:6a860ea136204e08fbb5ac4b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Scopa (Italian: [ˈskoːpa]\; lit. 'broom') is a century old t
 raditional Italian card game\, involving memory\, skill\, strategy and lit
 tle bit of luck. It is easy to learn\, and a challenge to master. Bring yo
 ur friends or make new ones while playing this classic pass time.
LOCATION:Humber Summit
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a860ea136204e08fbb5ac4b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
