BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Death Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T200000
UID:69e8db79cdd2f7e31fe2e42f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A Death Café is a gathering of people\, often strangers\, who
  will drink tea\, have a snack and discuss death together. The aim is to i
 ncrease the awareness of death with a view to helping people make the most
  of their lives. Discussions will be in small groups with no agenda\, no o
 bjectives and no particular theme. Prepare to hear and tell stories.\nThis
  is not a grief support or counselling session. The facilitator for this D
 eath Café is Sharon Lazenby.\nDrop-in\, but space is limited.
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8db79cdd2f7e31fe2e42f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
