BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
UID:6a774d824523092f0035ae9e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\\\nBeyond the Now\nWhat if the future isn't so
 mething that happens to us—but something we can shape? Explore bold idea
 s\, inspiring innovators and practical solutions that challenge us to thin
 k beyond today and imagine a better tomorrow. Closed Captions. 53 minutes.
  2024.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a774d824523092f0035ae9e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T160000
UID:6a774c9af4e5db3d00c75042@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\nThe Last Surviving Cheetahs\nThis film follow
 s the search for the critically endangered Asiatic cheetah in the remote d
 eserts of Iran. This powerful documentary captures the struggle to protect
  one of the world’s rarest big cats before it disappears forever. 55 min
 utes. 2025
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a774c9af4e5db3d00c75042
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
