BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seeing War Art Through Canadian Veterans' Stories
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T200000
UID:6a5e63640ed7b4521ed694a0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​How do we see war—and what changes when we listen to thos
 e who lived it? Drawing on interviews with Canadian veterans of the Battle
  of Ortona\, this illustrated talk explores how their memories of combat\,
  responsibility\, and uncertainty can reshape how we understand well-known
  works of Canadian war art.\nPresented by Ian Cosh\, author of ​\nGhosts
  of Ortona\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Floor 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e63640ed7b4521ed694a0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
