DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T170000
UID:69c1d0efbfe6da1042250aff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Tuesday afternoon from 2 pm-5 p
 m.\nVisit our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrossc
 ultural.org.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease
  bring your immigration documents (PR card) with you
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0efbfe6da1042250aff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult and Senior's Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T153000
UID:6a7bb844be1482002986b766@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and join our adult and senior's social as we engage in v
 arious activities\, games and crafts. Relax\, have fun\, and learn somethi
 ng new while connecting with new friends. This is a drop-in program.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7bb844be1482002986b766
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T170000
UID:69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Movies: Gilda (1946)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T160000
UID:69b1e74b4dacf581ff8146ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an afternoon of classic movies. Tea & coffee will 
 be served.\nGilda (1946)\nA small-time gambler hired to work in a Buenos A
 ires casino discovers his employer's new wife is his former lover.\nNo reg
 istration required.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1e74b4dacf581ff8146ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Retirement Planning and Living
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
UID:6a2757984407827f8aa38eb3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:It's never too late to start thinking about investing! Managin
 g your finances to maximize your retirement years is the goal of retiremen
 t planning. Your retirement strategy should strike a balance between your 
 financial realities\, requirements and wants. This presentation will cover
  how to plan for retirement\, sources of retirement income and how to prot
 ect yourself from scams\, frauds and financial abuse.\nPresented by Canadi
 an Investment Regulatory Organization (CIRO)\, a national self-regulatory 
 organization that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers an
 d trading activity on Canada’s debt and equity marketplaces.\nhttps://ww
 w.ciro.ca/about-ciro\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2757984407827f8aa38eb3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T153000
UID:6a832092aafa6100295d27ee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on basic keyboard functions for absolute beginners wit
 h little or no computer experience.\nIn this second session you will:\nFam
 iliarize yourself through practice with the most essential keyboard functi
 ons (alphabet\, number and symbol keys)\nPractice proper keyboarding postu
 re\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use a keyboard 
 at a beginner level and know how to go online for additional practice.\nPr
 erequisites: Computer for Beginners 1 or basic mouse skills\nFormat: Hands
 -on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a832092aafa6100295d27ee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
