BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3D Design With OnShape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T160000
UID:6a594d0f88e9bf2800315e7a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class introduces participants to a simple but useful tool
  - Onshape. This program allows users to create 3-dimensional objects with
  simple geometric shapes. The program is available for free and runs in-br
 owser.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a594d0f88e9bf2800315e7a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quick and Healthy Meal Prep to Simplify Your Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T200000
UID:6a85e126f564ef0d72c0f1f8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn a new recipe and how to put together a healthy\, homemad
 e meal. Chef Carolina will provide food and nutrition insights\, and demon
 strate how anyone can effortlessly put a meal together\, how to meal plan 
 to save time and money\, and have a nutritionally balanced diet. This prog
 ram will be a demonstration of food preparation and assembly of pre-cooked
  items into a completed dish.  No actual oven or stovetop cooking will be 
 taking place during the program.\nFood allergy notice\n: Please be aware t
 hat food will be used in this program. Food products used in this program 
 may contain or may have come into contact with common allergens. (*Contain
 s dairy\, sugar\, and caffeine)\n*Registration Required. Space is limited.
 \nRegister online or call 416-396-8872.\nRegistration opens October 5\, 20
 26\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e126f564ef0d72c0f1f8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
