UID:6a3e941a86636e3d0050d4e4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join other handicraft hobbyists to share ideas\, skills\, and 
 stories while you work on your own projects. Whether you knit\, crochet\, 
 cross-stitch\, etc.\, drop in for light refreshments and great conversatio
 ns with other crafters.\nPlease bring your own projects and materials\, as
  this is\nnot a class\n\, and no supplies are available\n. Limited assista
 nce is available for most needlework hobbies. All skill levels are welcome
 .\nFor adults and older adults. Registration is\noptional\nif you would li
 ke reminders. Please register online\, in-branch\, or call\n416-396-8964\n
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Goldhawk Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e941a86636e3d0050d4e4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
