DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T160000
UID:6a7b4baf86ec588db26fd6ed@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors Digital Literacy\nis a\n6-week course\ndesigned to bui
 ld your confidence by introducing new skills slowly. At the end of the cou
 rse\, you may not know everything about the internet\, but you will have a
 \nsolid foundation\nof\nnew skills\nand the\nconfidence\nto continue learn
 ing.\nIs This Course Right for You?\nFor seniors: beginners\, with\nvery\n
 limited or\nno\ncomputer experience\n*6 weeks:\nwith 1 class and 1 practic
 e session weekly (practice sessions take place on Thursdays from 2:00-3:30
 pm for the duration of the course)\n*Excluding the week of October 12th du
 e to the holiday closure.\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such as the m
 ouse and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, services and
  entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and friends\
 nThe class is limited to 10 participants.  Please visit Richview Library 
 to fill out an application form.
LOCATION:Richview\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b4baf86ec588db26fd6ed
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: Remembering Gene Wilder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T200000
UID:6a752a363f18b57d52340398@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The loving tribute to Gene Wilder celebrates his life and lega
 cy as the comic genius behind an extraordinary string of film roles\, from
  his first collaboration with Mel Brooks in The Producers to the enigmatic
  title role in the original Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory to his i
 nspired on-screen partnership with Richard Pryor in movies like Silver Str
 eak. It is Illustrated by a bevy of touching and hilarious clips and outta
 kes\, never-before-seen home movies\, narration from Wilder's audiobook me
 moir\, and interviews with a roster of brilliant friends and collaborators
  like Mel Brooks\, Alan Alda\, and Carol Kane.\nDrop in!
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a752a363f18b57d52340398
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
