BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Medicine Workshop: Cedar Salve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T150000
UID:6a580ca8e9de6536001bfb85@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, participants will learn about the significa
 nce of Cedar from an Indigenous perspective\, including its use as a t
 raditional medicine and its beneficial properties. Attendees will also mak
 e a cedar salve to take home! All supplies will be provided.\nThe program
  will be capped at the first 15 participants.\nTanya Gluvakov is a mixed M
 ohawk woman from Toronto with family and "roots" from Six Nations of the G
 rand River in Oshweken\, Ontario. The founder of Roots and Raven\, Tanya i
 s a herbalist\, a mom\, a teacher\, and auntie\, who teaches several works
 hops about medicines from the land and how connecting with them helps us f
 ind our way. She also leads several projects that bring the resurgence of 
 medicines and accessibility to urban communities\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd fl.
