BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T113000
UID:6a5144f517f387c203a4af69@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse\nA class on how to us
 e a mouse for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nI
 n this first session you will:\nObserve and practice how to operate a mous
 e effectively\nUnderstand various mouse pointers and cursors\nReview basic
  keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for basic Windows functions\nUpon compl
 etion of this class students will be able to use a computer mouse at a bas
 ic level and will be able to go online for additional practice.\nComputers
  for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard\nA class on basic keyboard functions fo
 r absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nIn this secon
 d session you will:\nFamiliarize yourself through practice with the most e
 ssential keyboard functions (alphabet\, number and symbol keys)\nPractice 
 proper keyboarding posture\nUpon completion of this class students will be
  able to use a keyboard at a beginner level and know how to go online for 
 additional practice.\nComputers for Beginners 3: Use the Internet\nAn intr
 oductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners with little computer
  experience.\nIn this fourth session you will:\nUnderstand how to read a w
 eb site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch for information usin
 g a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to understand its key comp
 onents\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use the int
 ernet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\nComputers for Beg
 inners 4: Use Google Search and Maps\nA class on using Google's filters\, 
 tools\, and Maps for absolute beginners with little computer experience.\n
 In this fifth session you will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively 
 to find websites\, images\, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find ad
 dresses and get directions for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion o
 f this class students will be able to use more advanced search engine feat
 ures and use Google Maps at a basic level.\nComputers for Beginners 5: Use
  Windows\nA class on essential basic Windows skills for absolute beginners
  with little computer experience.\nIn this third session you will:\nBecome
  familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using common Wi
 ndows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, Applications
 \nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understanding o
 f how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.
LOCATION:McGregor Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5144f517f387c203a4af69
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Group Art Therapy with the Alzheimer Society of Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T153000
UID:6a594f8388e9bf2800315ff0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join this four-part Group Art Therapy series! Through individu
 al and collaborative creative activities\, participants will have the oppo
 rtunity to explore and express thoughts\, feelings\, and experiences in a 
 supportive and welcoming environment. Using a variety of artistic material
 s and mediums\, the group will discover new ways to connect\, reflect\, an
 d communicate through the creative process. No previous art experience is 
 required.\nThis program series is presented in collaboration with the Alzh
 eimer Society of Toronto and is designed for people living with early to m
 id stage dementia or mild cognitive impairment\, or together with a care p
 artner.\nAbout the facilitator: Kathleen Downie is an arts educator who ha
 s led many engaging art programs with the Alzheimer Society of Toronto ove
 r the years. Kathleen is currently completing her Art Therapy training thr
 ough the Vancouver Art Therapy Institute (VATI) Distance Program. As part 
 of her training\, Kathleen will facilitate group art therapy sessions for 
 individuals living with mild to moderate dementia or mild cognitive impair
 ment (MCI)\, along with their care partners.\nSnacks are provided for all 
 participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThe Alzh
 eimer Society of Toronto is solely responsible for the protection of perso
 nal information collected through the program registration process. Regist
 ration closes after week 1\, or when full.\nLINK\nhttps://alz.to/calendar/
 group-art-therapy-with-kathleen/2026-08-10/\nThis program is a Collaborati
 ve program with the Alzheimer Society of Toronto and Toronto Public Librar
 y.
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a594f8388e9bf2800315ff0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
