BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Innovation Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T200000
UID:69aeef0ab0595799c0a1e605@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Conversation is the source of innovation!\nJoin TPL Innovation
  Council member\nZahra Ebrahim\nfor a series of lively book discussions ab
 out how we can build a better world by getting better at talking with eac
 h other.\nOur September book is\nHow Minds Change\n\, by David McRaney. I
 n the lead-up to municipal elections this October\, we can expect public d
 iscourse to polarize along political lines. How can we have discussions th
 at change people's minds? And should we?\nFrom "Deep Canvassing" efforts t
 o raise support for gay marriage in the U.S. one voter at a time\, to an 
 analysis of how social change happens on a mass scale\, How Minds Change
  takes a fast-paced\, well-researched look at the science of persuasion.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69aeef0ab0595799c0a1e605
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
