BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wildlife-friendly Fall Gardens Presented on the behalf of the Davi
 d Suzuki Foundation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T190000
UID:6a8753c9aafa6100295df458@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At this time of year\, many people admire the fall colours but
  also feel the need to rake and dispose of leaves\, cut dead stems\, and r
 emove fallen branches. But what if this tidying up negatively affects our 
 gardens and pollinators? While we may not see the bees and butterflies dur
 ing the fall and winter\, they are still around!\nIn this presentation\, l
 earn about how to maintain and protect wildlife habitat even throughout th
 e colder months\, and how “leave the leaves” can help nature come back
  stronger the next season.\nPresented by\nDorte Windmuller\n\, a Butterfly
 way Ranger of the\nDavid Suzuki Foundation (DSF)\nas part of TPL’s envir
 onmental program series\, Our Fragile Plant.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nf Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8753c9aafa6100295df458
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
