BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connecting the Dots(?) Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
UID:6a11b72b8e677a28001e0617@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered why people believe in conspiracies?\nIn
  this book club\, we will be reading books that explore the social conditi
 ons that make people prone to extreme belief.\nThurs. Jun. 11\, 2:00-4:00p
 m\nEscaping the Rabbit Hole by Mick West\nThurs. Jul 9\, 2:00-4:00pm\nBlac
 k Pill by Elle Reeve\nThurs. Aug. 13\, 2:00-4:00pm\nProject Mind Control b
 y John Lisle\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Sept. 10\, 2:00-4:00pm\nConspiracy: 
 Peter Thiel\, Hulk Hogan\, Gawker\, and the Anatomy of Intrigue by Ryan Ho
 liday\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Oct. 8\, 2:00-4:00pm\nThe Brainwashing of M
 y Dad by Jen Senko\nThurs. Nov. 12\, 2:00-4:00pm\nShock Doctrine by Naomi 
 Klein
