DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T143000
UID:6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7946@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the following Monday afternoons to discuss books i
 n a friendly and social atmosphere: September 14th\, October 19th\, Novemb
 er 9th\, and December 14th.\nThis month we will be reading and discussing\
 nEmpire of Pain\nby Patrick Radden Keefe\n.\nEmpire of Pain\nby Patrick Ra
 dden Keefe is a gripping nonfiction account of the Sackler family\, whose 
 immense wealth and influence were built through Purdue Pharma and the mark
 eting of OxyContin. Blending investigative journalism\, family saga\, and 
 social history\, the book explores the rise of a powerful dynasty and its 
 central role in the opioid crisis. This thought-provoking read raises impo
 rtant questions about corporate responsibility\, wealth\, power\, and acco
 untability.\nParticipants can borrow a copy of the book from the Woodside 
 Square branch upon registration.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7946
