BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Sachet Embroidery Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T153000
UID:6a873fe14cb69d003e221bf6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn three different embroidery stitches while creating a sim
 ple embroidered lavender flower on a piece of linen. Then sew the embroide
 ry into a small sachet filled with lavender from the fields of Norfolk cou
 nty.\nAlong the way\, participants will gain confidence with basic embroid
 ery techniques and hand-sewing skills. Spot are limited\, registration req
 uired.\n----------\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informati
 on on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publi
 c Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will
  only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation
 . Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
  to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge St
 reet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a873fe14cb69d003e221bf6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NEW DATE: Runnymede Film Club Presents: Saturday Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T200000
UID:69fd15ecc7d3cd580057bf67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a monthly film screening of\nSaturday Night\n(2024
 \, Rated R).\nAt 11:30 pm on October 11\, 1975\, a ferocious troupe of you
 ng comedians and writers changed television\, and culture\, forever. This 
 film is based on the true story of what happened behind the scenes in the 
 90 minutes leading up to the first broadcast of Saturday Night Live.\nDrop
 -in.\n*Please note\, this program will now take place on Tuesday\, August 
 25th from 6-8 pm.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd15ecc7d3cd580057bf67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
