BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maintaining an Engaging and Enjoyable Backyard During the Winter S
 eason: Strategies for Feeding Birds in Colder Months
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T150000
UID:6a39632a414ef43d0097ade1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When temperatures drop and natural food becomes less available
 \, it's important to keep your backyard welcoming for birds. By adjusting 
 your feeding habits during colder months\, you can make winter feeding eas
 ier for yourself and help maintain a lively outdoor space that brings you 
 daily pleasure. J\nim Mackiewicz is the owner of Wild Birds Unlimited and 
 has been helping customers with backyard bird feeding and connecting to na
 ture for 25 years.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informati
 on on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publi
 c Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will
  only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation
 . Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
  to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge St
 reet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a39632a414ef43d0097ade1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beaches Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:696be0372c65973d001863f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the months book pick in 
 a welcoming\, relaxed setting. New members are always welcome and encourag
 ed to join.\nJanuary 8 - The Story of Us by Catherine Hernandez\nFebruary 
 5 - Death of the Author by Nnedi Okarofor\nMarch 5 - Wuthering Heights by 
 Emily Bronte\nApril 2 - The Siren's Call by Chris Hayes\nMay 7 - That Time
  I Loved You by Carianne Leung\nJune 4 - Any Other Way: How Toronto Got Qu
 eer by John Lorinc\nJuly 2 - The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy by Dougl
 as Adams\nAugust 6 - Demon Copperhead by Barbara Kingsolver\nSeptember 3 -
  Noopiming by Leanne Betasamosake Simpson\nOctober 1 - Shadow of the Wind 
 by Carlos Ruiz Zafon\nNovember 5 - House Divided by Alex Bozikovic\nDecemb
 er 3 - The Glass Hotel by Emily St. John Mandel\nCopies of our book club p
 icks will be set aside each month at the first-floor desk at Beaches Libra
 ry. These titles are also available as eBooks and eAudiobooks through Libb
 y\, and in alternate formats.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
