BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reading Challenge Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T210000
UID:69921264b48451fc3c02eb49@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Each month we will explore and discuss a title that falls into
  one of the TPL Reading Challenge categories.\nThis month we will be disc
 ussing\nBanyan Moon\nby Thao Thai\nCategory Is – Dual Perspectives\nThre
 e Vietnamese American women mourning the death of the family matriarch rec
 ount their lives and childhoods at a crumbling\, gothic manor called Banya
 n House\, where the secrets of her grandmother's past come to light.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Centre of room at Canoe Table
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69921264b48451fc3c02eb49
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care: The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T150000
UID:6a626ecff213992f00c682d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This author talk will address the experiences of families who 
 are caring for a loved one who is living with dementia\, including the var
 ious points of stress\, as well as the various points of joy\, and ways in
  which caregivers learn to survive the experience. Major topics include un
 derstanding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved one\, choosing an
  assisted living facility\, and using music and the arts as a means of con
 nection.\nPresented by Grant Campbell\, author of "\nSurviving Dementia Ca
 re\n: The Realities of Family Caregiving" (University of Toronto Press\, 
 2026).\nThe author will have copies of the book available for purchase and
  signing.
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a626ecff213992f00c682d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Privacy 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T153000
UID:6a020e77f56bd86e00aeefd6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested to learn how to maintain your online privac
 y and how to secure your online accounts and devices? If so\, this is the 
 class for you. Come and join us in this introductory session that is fille
 d with hands-on activities and discussion.\nIn this program\, you will:\nL
 earn how to maintain your online privacy through good habits and the secur
 ity of your accounts and devices.\nDevelop a strong password\, and review 
 the best methods for storing your passwords.\nLearn about various online t
 hreats: malware\, phishing\, hacking\, etc.\nGain an understanding of the 
 limitations of these tools and habits.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8\nAccessibility\nLive or auto
 mated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, intervenor servic
 es\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your 
 request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a020e77f56bd86e00aeefd6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
