BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beaches Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T200000
UID:696be0372c65973d001863f6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the months book pick in 
 a welcoming\, relaxed setting. New members are always welcome and encourag
 ed to join.\nJanuary 8 - The Story of Us by Catherine Hernandez\nFebruary 
 5 - Death of the Author by Nnedi Okarofor\nMarch 5 - Wuthering Heights by 
 Emily Bronte\nApril 2 - The Siren's Call by Chris Hayes\nMay 7 - That Time
  I Loved You by Carianne Leung\nJune 4 - Any Other Way: How Toronto Got Qu
 eer by John Lorinc\nJuly 2 - The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy by Dougl
 as Adams\nAugust 6 - Demon Copperhead by Barbara Kingsolver\nSeptember 3 -
  Noopiming by Leanne Betasamosake Simpson\nOctober 1 - Shadow of the Wind 
 by Carlos Ruiz Zafon\nNovember 5 - House Divided by Alex Bozikovic\nDecemb
 er 3 - The Glass Hotel by Emily St. John Mandel\nCopies of our book club p
 icks will be set aside each month at the first-floor desk at Beaches Libra
 ry. These titles are also available as eBooks and eAudiobooks through Libb
 y\, and in alternate formats.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Enigmatic Elders Mystery Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T150000
UID:6a347954f56bd86e00b7ad6e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This book club is for readers who enjoy reading various types 
 of mysteries. Meetings will be held every\nthird Thursday\nof each month.\
 nOur goal is to have fun and travel the reading journey together.\nWe will
  be covering the following 4 books on the following dates:\nDeath in Focus
 \nby Anne Perry\n(September 17th) ~ 1st floor\, Founders Room\nThe Mystery
  Writer\nby Sulari Gentill\n(October 15th) ~ 1st floor\, Founders Room\nTh
 e Hanging Girl\nby Jussi Adler-Olsen\n(November 19th) ~ 3rd floor\, Discus
 sion Room\nPoirot's Christmas\nby Agatha Christie\n(December 17th) ~ 3rd f
 loor\, Discussion Room\nNOTE\n: Contact us three weeks prior the next mee
 ting if you require a\nlarge print\ncopy\, if available.\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@
 tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 1st Floor\, Founders Room (across fro
 m Beeton Hall Auditorium)
