BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ACT-ively Preventing Elder Abuse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260902T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260902T150000
UID:6a6a38590e562e28009d4f27@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Break down the stigma around elder abuse and learn how to reco
 gnize and respond to it in a safe way. Join a facilitator from Theatre of 
 the Beat for this practical and engaging workshop where you'll learn to:\n
 identify the different types of elder abuse\nIdentify the signs of elder a
 buse\nUsing theatre exercises\, develop strategies to be an 'active      b
 ystander' in situations where elder abuse might be present. No theatre    
   experience required\, but participation in role plays is encouraged!\nAb
 out Theatre of the Beat:\nTheatre of the Beat (TOTB) is a Canadian touring
  theatre company working to catalyze conversations on social justice and i
 ts intersection with the beliefs of the communities in which we find ourse
 lves.\nLight refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient li
 sts will be available at the program.\nDrop-in program\, registration not 
 required.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a38590e562e28009d4f27
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
