SUMMARY:Death Café Open - Conversation About Death
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T200000
UID:6a7f4c05d4b10d0030067add@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a welcoming discussion group where people gather t
 o talk openly about death. This is not a grief support or counselling sess
 ion\, but a space for meaningful\, thoughtful conversations that many part
 icipants find surprisingly profound.\nHosted by Jacqueline:\nShe is passio
 nate about creating spaces for honest conversations about end-of-life awar
 eness. With 20+ years of experience as an Educator\, Holistic Coach\, and 
 Reiki Master\, she supports individuals and families in approaching end-of
 -life preparation with awareness\, compassion\, and grace. Snacks and refr
 eshment are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availa
 ble at the program.\nRegistration required.
