BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afternoon Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T143000
UID:6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7947@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the following Monday afternoons to discuss books i
 n a friendly and social atmosphere: September 14th\, October 19th\, Novemb
 er 9th\, and December 14th.\nThis month we will be reading\nMartyr!\nby Ka
 veh Akbar.\nMartyr!\nis the 2024 debut novel by Iranian-American poet Kave
 h Akbar. It is a\nNew York Times\nbestseller and the paper's 2024 "Best Bo
 oks of the Year So Far." It was a finalist for the 2024\nWaterstones Debut
  Fiction Prize\nand shortlisted for the\nNational Book Award for\nFiction
 .\nThe novel follows Cyrus Shams\, a newly sober\, queer\, Iranian-America
 n who becomes consumed with the idea of martyrdom. With the musculature of
  poetry and incandescent ideas\, images\, and humour\, the novel is an ine
 dible and haunted searching. Guided by the voices of lost artists\, poets\
 , and kings\, Cyrus embarks on a search that leads him to a terminally il
 l painter living out her final days in the Brooklyn Museum.\nParticipants 
 can borrow a copy of the book from the Woodside Square branch upon registr
 ation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7947
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
