BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care: The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T143000
UID:6a6d6326e9de6536001fb0c3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This author talk will address the experiences of families who 
 are caring for a loved one who is living with dementia\, including the var
 ious points of stress\, as well as the various points of joy\, and ways in
  which caregivers learn to survive the experience. Major topics include un
 derstanding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved one\, choosing an
  assisted living facility\, and using music and the arts as a means of con
 nection.\nPresented by Grant Campbell\, author of "\nSurviving Dementia Ca
 re\n: The Realities of Family Caregiving" (University of Toronto Press\, 
 2026).\nThe author will have copies of the book available for purchase and
  signing.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6d6326e9de6536001fb0c3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer of Fear '77: The Murder of Shoeshine Boy Emanuel Jaques
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T200000
UID:6a4eda9bfb418a2800999ac1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Investigative journalist Robert J. Hoshowsky (\nOutraged: the 
 Murder of Shoeshine Boy\, Emanuel Jaques\n) examines the shocking abductio
 n and murder of a 12-year-old boy that enraged a nation and forced the shu
 tdown of Yonge Street’s sex trade.\nThe discovery of Emanuel Jaques’ r
 emains on the rooftop of a Yonge Street massage parlour on August 1\nst\n\
 , 1977\, ignited a firestorm. Within a few days\, thousands descended on T
 oronto City Hall demanding the reinstatement of capital punishment\, which
  had just been abolished a year earlier.\nFed-up with countless sex shops\
 , strip clubs and X-rated movie theatres\, the public\, politicians and bu
 sinesses demanded change. This resulted in the most sweeping clean-up in C
 anadian history\, which remains controversial to this day.\nThe author wil
 l have copies of the newly-released\, second edition of his book for sal
 e:\nOutrage: the Murder of Shoeshine Boy Emanuel Jaques\n(ISBN 1069337404)
 .
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4eda9bfb418a2800999ac1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
