DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T160000
UID:6a7745ccf4e5db3d00c74d7a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will 
 be available upon request.\nPompeii’s Secret Underworld\nFor more than 2
 00 years\, Pompeii has been celebrated by archaeologists as a refined city
  at the center of a highly advanced ancient civilization. But recent excav
 ations are revealing a far more complex story about the city that was cata
 strophically buried when Mount Vesuvius erupted in 79 CE. Closed Captions.
 55 min. 2025
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7745ccf4e5db3d00c74d7a
