DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T190000
UID:6a7b6cd877177f0030621047@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Winter is a harsh season\, yet many birds stay in Toronto and 
 survive. Why don’t they all fly south? How do they stay warm? Which bird
 s stay and which ones migrate? Learn about migrant birds and their incredi
 ble journeys\, visiting birds who come to the city from their boreal and A
 rctic homes\, and our resident birds who spend the cold winter months here
 .\nJoin Monika Croydon\, avid local birder and member of the Toronto Ornit
 hological Club\, to find out how we can all help birds in winter\, from pr
 oviding feeders and creating bird-friendly gardens and homes\, to supporti
 ng conservation and research as Citizen Scientists.\nPlease register onlin
 e.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
